    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGE5NDdiOTM4MGY0NWY3MGJjODAxZDE0MTEwOTUzYjg4NGQyYTc0NDQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T19:06:04Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-08T19:06:04Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(setup): the setup defines the work offset, not each height\n\nA height measured from the work offset no longer names its own slot:\nHeightReference::WorkOffset is a unit variant that resolves through\nsetup::wcs_slot (the setup's pick, else G54) - the same law the post\nreads, so an operation cannot disagree with its setup.\n\n- Heights page: no per-height WCS combo; a read-only \"Work offset\" row\n  shows the setup's word and points to the Setups page.\n- Project v52: the v51 -> v52 rung lifts per-height slots onto their\n  setup when the setup agreed (posting and stamps unchanged), and\n  refuses the load by name (WorkOffsetConflict, listing each op and its\n  slots) when they disagreed or a setup-less document named a non-G54\n  slot. A v52 height carrying a slot is corrupt; the MCP params door\n  refuses one too.\n- The #196 per-op \"height on another slot\" post refusal is gone (the\n  conflict cannot be built); the one-file shared-word refusal stays.\n- Setups page \"Auto\" reads \"G54 (default)\"; the setup sheet says\n  \"program offset: G54 (the default - not picked)\"; the viewport plane\n  chip names the setup's word.\n\nDecision record: docs/decisions/329-setup-defines-wcs.md.\n\nFixes #329\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
